    "farms": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<style>\n.story-farms { background: #FFF8F0; padding: 2rem 0 4rem; }\n.story-farm {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n  gap: 0;\n  max-width: 1200px;\n  margin: 0 auto 3rem;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(61,35,20,0.08);\n}\n.story-farm:nth-child(even) .story-farm__img-wrap { order: 2; }\n.story-farm:nth-child(even) .story-farm__content { order: 1; }\n@media (max-width: 749px) {\n  .story-farm { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .story-farm:nth-child(even) .story-farm__img-wrap { order: 0; }\n  .story-farm:nth-child(even) .story-farm__content { order: 0; }\n}\n.story-farm__img-wrap { position: relative; min-height: 350px; }\n.story-farm__img {\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  object-fit: cover;\n}\n.story-farm__content {\n  padding: 3rem 2.5rem;\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  justify-content: center;\n  background: #F5EDE4;\n}\n.story-farm__name {\n  font-family: var(--font-heading-family);\n  font-size: 1.6rem;\n  color: #3D2314;\n  margin: 0 0 0.25rem;\n  font-weight: 400;\n}\n.story-farm__location {\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  letter-spacing: 0.15em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: #D4956A;\n  margin-bottom: 1.25rem;\n}\n.story-farm__desc {\n  font-size: 0.95rem;\n  line-height: 1.8;\n  color: #5a3e2e;\n  margin: 0;\n}\n</style>\n<div class=\"story-farms page-width\">\n  <div class=\"story-farm\">\n    <div class=\"story-farm__img-wrap\">\n      <img class=\"story-farm__img\" src=\"{{ 'story-cacao-pods.jpg' | asset_url }}\" alt=\"Ripe cacao pods at Finca Cacayo\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"story-farm__content\">\n      <h3 class=\"story-farm__name\">Finca Cacayo</h3>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__location\">Highland Region, Honduras</p>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__desc\">Nestled in the misty highlands at 800 metres, Finca Cacayo produces some of the rarest Criollo beans in Central America. The volcanic soil and cool mountain air give their cacao delicate floral notes you won&rsquo;t find anywhere else. Third-generation farmer Don Miguel tends each tree by hand.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"story-farm\">\n    <div class=\"story-farm__img-wrap\">\n      <img class=\"story-farm__img\" src=\"{{ 'story-farmer-hands.jpg' | asset_url }}\" alt=\"Women farmers sorting cacao beans at La Campesina cooperative\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"story-farm__content\">\n      <h3 class=\"story-farm__name\">La Campesina</h3>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__location\">Women-Led Cooperative, Guatemala</p>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__desc\">La Campesina is run entirely by women &mdash; 23 families who chose organic farming long before it was trendy. Their beans have a rich, fruity depth with hints of red berries. Every purchase supports their community school and healthcare programme.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"story-farm\">\n    <div class=\"story-farm__img-wrap\">\n      <img class=\"story-farm__img\" src=\"{{ 'story-farm-aerial.jpg' | asset_url }}\" alt=\"Aerial view of Finca Las Delias cacao plantation\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"story-farm__content\">\n      <h3 class=\"story-farm__name\">Finca Las Delias</h3>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__location\">Pacific Lowlands, Nicaragua</p>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__desc\">Three generations of the Delgado family have farmed this land. The rich volcanic soil of the Pacific lowlands produces beans with deep, earthy chocolate notes and a smooth, lingering finish. They pioneered regenerative farming practices in their region.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"story-farm\">\n    <div class=\"story-farm__img-wrap\">\n      <img class=\"story-farm__img\" src=\"{{ 'story-rainforest.jpg' | asset_url }}\" alt=\"Shade-grown cacao under native rainforest canopy at Hacienda La Luz\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"story-farm__content\">\n      <h3 class=\"story-farm__name\">Hacienda La Luz</h3>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__location\">Rainforest Reserve, Costa Rica</p>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__desc\">At La Luz, cacao grows the way nature intended &mdash; under the shade of native rainforest trees. Their shade-grown approach protects biodiversity while producing beans with complex, nutty flavour profiles. They maintain 40 hectares of protected primary forest.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"story-farm\">\n    <div class=\"story-farm__img-wrap\">\n      <img class=\"story-farm__img\" src=\"{{ 'story-beans-drying.jpg' | asset_url }}\" alt=\"Cacao beans drying in the sun at Hacienda RC\" loading=\"lazy\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"story-farm__content\">\n      <h3 class=\"story-farm__name\">Hacienda RC</h3>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__location\">Cacao Heritage Region, Belize</p>\n      <p class=\"story-farm__desc\">Hacienda RC is on a mission to preserve heirloom Criollo varieties that have been cultivated in Belize for centuries. Their ancient cacao genetics produce beans with unparalleled complexity &mdash; notes of honey, tobacco, and dark fruit that no modern hybrid can match.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "padding_top": 0,
        "padding_bottom": 0
      }
